    {
      "id": "aLJB",
      "code_hash": "136f83a19bc83477bc7f596685392cae",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.75rem'>\n    <div style=\"font-size:0.9375rem;color:#5d5e61\">\n      <p style=\"color:#1b1c1e;margin:0 0 0.4rem\">\n        Things a scan cannot see, which somebody has to answer.\n      </p>\n      <ul style=\"margin:0 0 1rem;padding-left:1.1rem\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3rem\">Measure the front doorway and send us the number<span style=\"color:#8a8a88\"> \u2014 Open the door all the way and measure from the face of the door across to the frame. That's the width a wheelchair actually gets, and it needs 32 inches.</span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3rem\">Send a photo of the front door handle<span style=\"color:#8a8a88\"> \u2014 Straight on, close enough to see its shape. We'll check it opens with a closed fist and sits between 34 and 48 inches up.</span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3rem\">Push the front door open with one finger and tell us if it gives<span style=\"color:#8a8a88\"> \u2014 A door should open with 5 pounds of push, and one finger is about right for that.</span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3rem\">Send a photo of the front doorway from the side<span style=\"color:#8a8a88\"> \u2014 Get the floor and the bottom of the door in frame. We'll measure the step and check it against the half inch the standard allows.</span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3rem\">Send a photo of the floor just inside the front door<span style=\"color:#8a8a88\"> \u2014 Include any mat. We'll check it lies flat, stays put, and that carpet is no thicker than half an inch.</span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3rem\">Send a photo of the customer restroom from the doorway<span style=\"color:#8a8a88\"> \u2014 Stand in the door and get the whole room in. We'll check there's a 60 inch circle to turn around in.</span></li></ul>\n      <p style=\"color:#1b1c1e;margin:0 0 0.4rem\">\n        Rules this room did not settle.\n      </p>\n      <ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:1.1rem\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3rem\">The way out is blocked<span style=\"color:#8a8a88\"> \u2014 waiting on the CBC 10 sections on accessible means of egress, including continuity and sizing requirements</span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3rem\">There is not enough room to turn this corner<span style=\"color:#8a8a88\"> \u2014 waiting on a turn with route either side of it to measure: one zone came back at zero</span></li></ul>\n    </div>\n    <marimo-ui-element object-id='BYtC-0' random-id='00abdf6c-8176-a5e1-cad9-028a56d186c0'><marimo-switch data-initial-value='true' data-label='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eRead every rule as verified, so every check runs&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;' data-disabled='false'></marimo-switch></marimo-ui-element><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Nobody has read a section on this machine yet, so these numbers come from thresholds no reviewer has confirmed. <code>standardphysics-agents rules review --by \"&lt;name&gt;\"</code> is where that happens.</span></span></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
