    {
      "id": "xXTn",
      "code_hash": "93ae638dc9ab5adf9b8c233df39b581a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"a-room-off-a-phone\">A room off a phone</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The shop above is geometry we authored, and authored geometry tests the\narithmetic without testing the assumptions. These rooms came off a phone.\nThe walls are where RoomPlan put them, the furniture is whatever it\nrecognised, and each piece carries a capture confidence: a check resting\non something the scan only glimpsed asks for another look instead of\nruling.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Nothing here is scored. Nobody measured these rooms by hand, so there is\nno correct answer to read the pipeline against. What you can see is what\nthe checks say about geometry that was measured rather than authored, and\nhow much of it the scan's own confidence holds back.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
